{
  "version": 1,
  "source": "Tests/RelayCoreTests/ConformanceTests.swift",
  "format": "{name, note, old?, new, cwd?, flags: [{kind, location, text}]}. The review's Look closer flags for the text `new` added or changed since `old` (every text of `new` when `old` is absent: a first view). A text is a step's or sub-step's code, url, detail or file, verify's the same, a link's url or path, or why; a text whose location holds the same value in `old` is skipped. Hosts and paths count as new only when `old` names them nowhere. location: \"step <id or path> code|url|detail|file\", \"verify code|…\", \"link <n> url|path\", \"why\". kind: pipeToShell, sudo, rmRf, decode, eval (command patterns, in code only), nonASCII (in code; in a host outside code), newHost (every http(s) host), absolutePathOutsideCwd (a file or link path starting with / or ~ outside `cwd`). text: the matched part, the host, the path, or the text with each non-ASCII character as ⟨U+XXXX⟩. Flags come per text in that order. Within a text: the command patterns in the order above, then the code's nonASCII, then for each host its newHost and (outside code) its nonASCII, then the path. An empty list is the no-match result, which the review shows as \"No pattern matched. These checks are incomplete.\"",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "look-no-match",
      "note": "plain text: no flag",
      "new": {
        "v": 1,
        "title": "Rotate the staging deploy key",
        "why": "The key is 90 days old.",
        "steps": [{"do": "Rotate the key", "id": "s1", "code": "deploy-key rotate --env staging"}]
      },
      "flags": []
    },
    {
      "name": "look-first-view-new-host",
      "note": "a first view flags every host",
      "new": {
        "v": 1,
        "title": "Rotate the staging deploy key",
        "steps": [
          {
            "do": "Open the deploy settings",
            "id": "s1",
            "url": "https://deploy.example.test/settings"
          }
        ],
        "links": [{"label": "Runbook", "url": "https://docs.example.test/runbook"}]
      },
      "flags": [
        {"kind": "newHost", "location": "step s1 url", "text": "deploy.example.test"},
        {"kind": "newHost", "location": "link 1 url", "text": "docs.example.test"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "look-host-already-named",
      "note": "a host the old version names anywhere is not new, though the text naming it is",
      "old": {
        "v": 1,
        "title": "Rotate the staging deploy key",
        "steps": [
          {
            "do": "Open the deploy settings",
